            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "katelikesfoods"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve made this recipe as written, and it turns out FANTASTIC. Rich, moist and full of flavor, this is definitely a dessert instead of breakfast or snack like I sometimes like to eat banana bread. Most recently I tried the recipe with the following modifications: half the white sugar, eliminated the cocoa powder and added a little extra flour, used plain Greek yogurt instead of sour cream, and butter instead of margarine. So good! I made one loaf and kept the chocolate chips in the recipe, and I used the other half of the batter to make muffins with crushed walnuts and spices. You can’t go wrong with this recipe!!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-13T21:06:09.983Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "A T"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I only had 3 large bananas so I halved the recipe. I used butter instead of margarine, 5% Fage yogurt instead of sour cream, full portions of vanilla and cocoa, and over a cup of milk chocolate chips. I also swirled in some peanut butter which made it very pretty and added some yummy richness. The combination was divine. I will definitely make it again!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-25T03:21:06.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Beckie Madden"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The first time I made this, I followed the recipe but halved the ingredients and made mini loaves (baked for 40 min). The only thing I didn't halve was the chocolate chips. The second time, I added some extra cocoa powder (3T instead of 2T) for more chocolatey goodness. The loaves were so moist and delicious, and I think this is a five star recipe even without modified amounts of chocolate! I will be making this many more times!!!",
            "datePublished": "2021-09-05T20:16:18.837Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SAG SUNSHINE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I sub'd olive oil instead of butter, left out the sour cream, baked in a Bundt pan for a little under an hour and five minutes. Don't let the color fool you; it's VERY moist!👏🏾👍🏾. In fact most of the time when a recipe calls for butter, i sub olive oil.",
            "datePublished": "2025-08-19T04:53:15.702Z"
          },
          {
